        <rdfs:comment>Some transporters, such as certain members of the SLC family, are referred to as &apos;carriers&apos;; however GO uses carrier with a different meaning: a carrier binds to and transports the substance (see GO:0140104 molecular carrier activity), whereas a transporter forms some pore that allows the passing of molecules.</rdfs:comment>
