    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0016192 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0016192">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cellular transport process in which transported substances are moved in membrane-bounded vesicles; transported substances are enclosed in the vesicle lumen or located in the vesicle membrane. The process begins with a step that directs a substance to the forming vesicle, and includes vesicle budding and coating. Vesicles are then targeted to, and fuse with, an acceptor membrane.</obo:IAO_0000115>
